  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Services and Opportunities for Host Communities and Displaced Rohingya Population</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The deveplment objective of the Bangladesh - Inclusive Services and Opportunities for Host Communities and Displaced Rohingya Population Project is to improve access to human capital services for vulnerable host communities and displaced Rohingya population. The project components consist of the following: Component 1: Building Community Resilience and Self-Reliance (US$30 million equivalent (credit); US$40 million equivalent (grant); Component 2: Supporting Education Opportunities for Children (US$40 million equivalent (credit); US$20 million equivalent (grant); Component 3: Enhancing Social Care and Economic Empowerment (US$25 million equivalent (credit); US$25 million equivalent (grant); Component 4: Healthier Communities (US$80 million equivalent (credit); US$55 million equivalent (grant); Component 5: GBV Response and Prevention (US$17.5 million equivalent (credit), US$17.5 million equivalent (grant); Component 6: Contingent Emergency Response (US$0 million).</narrative>
  </description>
